 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Lots of them, but the simple ones always work best. Do you have a dedicated work space, or do you end up where the world finds you? It does matter. Try doing some light stretching or standing up every twenty minutes. Also, leave your phone across the room while you start. You can ask them nicely if you can work after them, or start early in morning when it's quiet. That's a nice escape route to have. It's quiet, you don't need a coat, and there are tea and paper breaks if you need them.",
